+# Continuous-time bridge campaign
+
+Target: establish the exact transfer law that approaches the supplied compact rotor Hamiltonian at fixed microscopic g, and seek a phase-relevant estimate uniform in temporal spacing and spatial volume. Fixed-step Euclidean Villain masslessness is not by itself a theorem for that Hamiltonian. The finite-clock version must retain the order N and its actual kinetic operator.
+
+Main e0ef7cf4633034a8c1e6d57f5812cc4275bf1349 supplies a provisional isotropic finite-clock covariance/masslessness theorem, a finite SU3 Wilson Hamiltonian limit, and a qutrit principal-flux positive transfer with extensive error. None claims this selected rotor/clock phase bridge. Read their exact assumptions and relevant open-PR source before asserting a new theorem.
+
+Premises: the supplied cubic gauge carrier, Haar or finite-clock measure, explicit couplings and external time step. No native law selection, physical clock or coupling is supplied by this work. Current four axioms and approved primitives remain unchanged.
+
+Success witness: a matching exact generator plus quantitative estimates surviving the stated anisotropic/volume limits. A mismatch is a narrow map failure; it does not prove absence of a physical phase or demand new axioms. An inconclusive outcome preserves the actual uniform estimate still missing.
+
+First decisive checks: character Fourier coefficients identify temporal kinetic energies; normalized spatial weights identify the magnetic potential. Compare the actual finite transfer with the proposed generator on a physical one-plaquette sector. Then test whether candidate defect bounds price temporal subdivisions in physical time.
+
+Continue personally to2026-09-16 13:45:03UTC, with derivations first. No subagents, main merge, audit verdict or premature stop at a milestone.
