+# Numerical history
+
+Attempt1 of the calibrated-transfer program completed all assertions. Personal output review then found that the J=0.1 crossover gap, about1.3e-41, was reported as2.9e-10 by subtractive roundoff in log(lambda) with lambda near1. The absolute assertion tolerance did not detect this relative-resolution failure. The original source and raw stdout/stderr are preserved.
+
+The corrected calculation evaluates the exact positive deficit1-lambda=2 E sin²(pi rK/N), then uses-log1p(-deficit)/delta. It does not loosen a tolerance or change the mathematical target. A follow-up relative crossover assertion is required so the same loss cannot pass unnoticed. Matrix semigroup products still use the positive Poisson eigenvalues; their comparison remains an absolute finite-dimensional diagnostic.
+
+## Block03 state-check history
+
+All failed sources and raw outputs remain in this packet. None is an independent audit.
+
+1. Attempt1 (source2c9a22ed0eb2a9fa380e8e6f4810e0f0860cfe0261478154adfccf2b5676ccb7) failed the chosen final Gibbs trace-distance target0.003. A separately labeled resolution diagnostic, with that assertion replaced by printing, found0.0030218784500990045 at N48 on the delta0.4/N path. The other two paths gave0.0027206640958637855 and0.0029855759981625724. The target was retained; N64 was added and the rotor comparison cutoff enlarged from28 to40 so the larger embedded clock fits. This is a finite-resolution failure, not a theorem counterexample.
+2. Attempt2 (sourceb0515c4c806cec2527b5413352857dd6e6e5c675706adcfde3bd444c2b2f9b0b) then failed a badly posed diagnostic asserting an absolute commutator norm above1e-8. At N64, delta2/N^3, the norm is9.479355162113757e-9; its ratio to delta^2 is162.854. The physical factors are noncommuting, but their commutator must approach zero as the time step shrinks. The diagnostic output is retained.
+3. Attempt3 added a full N^4-angle-space, four-matter-state comparison at N3 and N4. A replacement lower threshold commutator/delta^2>1 was itself unjustified for these additional small clocks and failed at N3 before the comparison. Its source is retained. No universal numerical lower coefficient follows from noncommutation.
+4. Attempt4 checks only that the commutator is resolved above1000 machine-epsilon times the factor norms. It completes the full angle/reduced comparisons and all spectral/Gibbs checks. The two representation errors are2.54e-15 and6.23e-15. At N64 the three Gibbs trace distances are0.00220739,0.00152683,0.00167673; ground-state squared overlaps are0.999999127,0.999999587,0.999999430. Rotor cutoff40 versus48 checks the first12 energies and partition function to2e-12. These are floating diagnostics without certified tail intervals.
+
+The completed Block03 source is eb8506e11d1fa57705977b8081ccceb7c0eaede88c15caa2bb827cb08a1cdfb5. Formula mutation attempt1 ran14 genuinely altered programs; each returned a nonzero status containing AssertionError. This includes restoration of Block02's lost tiny-gap computation, reversed charged offsets/winding, an unsandwiched transfer, wrong Gauss charge, and omitted Gibbs normalization. The altered sources and raw streams are under review/formula_mutations. Mutation rejection tests sensitivity to these faults, not the truth of the general theorem.
